<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices fell on rising arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices fell on rising arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices on Tuesday were down on increased arrivals against limited buying from processing plants, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices were down by 100-200 rupees per tonne. Business was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices remained bearish and were down by 300 rupees per tonne on heavy selling pressure. The undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in thin trade. Soymeal yellow was $320-321 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $120-121 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 4,250 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. The undertone was easy.</p>
